From d6b803e70c96ef87e4109143f672acdd5f6eebc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:14:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] WIP HC16: native-bf16 producers for the remaining
 HC/attention activations

Generalises the bf16-copy emission.  The graph optimizer now marks the activation
(src1 root) of every MMB dense prefill GEMM "wants a BF16 copy", and the fused
rms_norm+mul, the fused sigmoid+mul (ggml_cuda_op_unary_mul), the fused
scale+unary and the generic unary all write that copy into slot 0 in addition to
the F32 output.  dsv4_hc_pre does the same for the HC mixed stream.  The GEMM's
activation conversion (mmb_cvt_f32_bf16) finds the copy in the slot and is
skipped.

The copies are RNE-rounded exactly as mmb_cvt_f32_bf16 and the F32 outputs stay
valid for every other consumer, so all gates stay bit-identical: PPL c2048
10.6428 unchanged, same-seed greedy text 9930c674a6ca unchanged,
FLASH_ATTN_QSA / GATED_DELTA_NET / FLASH_ATTN_EXT pass, W=1..8 width probe pure
(maxdiff 0).

LLAMA_MMB_CVT_LOG=1 now shows only the ple_embd model-tensor conversion, down
from the hc_norm / hc_mixed / final_output / attn_gated / unary families (and the
op-name fix shows the last family is unary, not MAP_CUSTOM1).

gfx1151 IQ4_XS Flash-Next, bf16 KV, -b/-ub 2048, MMB+QSA3 on:
pp8192 951.6 -> 963.7 (+1.3%), pp2048 977.1 -> 996.7 (+2.0%), HC16=1 vs 0.
